{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And you, take for yourself the finest spices.</b> Above, in parashat תְּצַוֶּה, I wrote that in every matter fit to be attributed in essence and primacy to Moses, the expression ״וְאַתָּה״ is used of it, and in this manner the expression ״וְאַתָּה״ is also used of the anointing oil, for it is made to anoint with it the Tabernacle and all its vessels, and Aaron and his sons, and all High Priests and kings, as is found in tractate Horayot (11a). And they said there that the oil that Moses made lasted forever, as it says: ״שֶׁמֶן מִשְׁחַת קֹדֶשׁ יִהְיֶה זֶה לִי לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם״ (Exodus 30:31). And all this is an allusion to what is said (Deuteronomy 33:21) ״וַיַּרְא רֵאשִׁית לוֹ״, which is expounded of Moses, for he was the רֵאשִׁית and beginning of all prophets and priests and kings and all kinds of rulership — all flowed from him, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Nedarim 38a): ״The Holy One, blessed be He, does not rest His Presence except upon one who is mighty, wise, rich, and humble — and all of them from Moses,״ which is to say that all of them received their eminence from Moses. Therefore one must liken oneself to him in his traits, for he was ״בִּישֻׁרוּן מֶלֶךְ״ (Deuteronomy 33:5) and ״בְּשָׂמִים רֹאשׁ״ — the head of all spices, for to him belongs the prerogative of רֵאשִׁית, and from him would flow the lamp of prophecy and the lamp of rulership, as it is written (Psalms 132:17) ״עָרַכְתִּי נֵר לִמְשִׁיחִי״. Therefore the weight of the spices was five hundred and its half two hundred and fifty, corresponding to two instances of נֵר, for at his source were found first of all two burning lamps, and from him every lamp would be kindled while he lacked nothing, for the face of Moses was like the sun that illuminates the earth and its inhabitants, and it lacks nothing and its light is constant and never diminishes forever. Thus said the Holy One, blessed be He: if you desire the permanence of this oil of anointing, then וְאַתָּה — you yourself, not through an agent — shall take it for yourself, for this special quality is given to you, that everything given through you lasts forever like the sun before Me, like the Torah given through you, which is eternal like the light of the sun. But the face of Joshua was like the moon, for he bequeathed the Land to Israel, and this gift is not eternal but like the moon, which is sometimes built up and sometimes breached. And therefore it says ״שֶׁמֶן מִשְׁחַת קֹדֶשׁ יִהְיֶה זֶה לִי לְדֹרֹתֵיכֶם״ (Exodus 30:31)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:24:31.698527758Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}